  "description": "A parametric SHOWER on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE ENCLOSURE IS THE PARAMETER THAT MATTERS. A shower in a corner needs two screens, one against a return wall needs one, and a wet room needs none — so the screens are a ternary over two quad rows, not three objects. The tray, the riser and every published figure are identical in all three.\n\nGLASS IS A REAL SOLID at its real thickness, on its own layer and colour. That is what lets the 3D read as an enclosure rather than a tray with a wall next to it, and it is why glass area comes out as a number a fitter can order against.\n\nSTEP HEIGHT is published because it is the figure that decides whether the tray is level-access, and it is the tray thickness — the one dimension people forget to check.",
